        "parms": "# ~adc and ~dac — a patch's audio in and out\nA ~dac is the patch's audio output: its left inlet is the left channel, its right inlet the right, passed on to whatever hosts the patch. A ~adc is the input: when the patch runs as an insert effect, its outlets carry the left and right channel of the audio it processes. A patch is silent until a signal reaches a ~dac.\nMax's adc~ and dac~ talk to the sound card, and take channel numbers as arguments. Here they talk to the bus the patch is placed on, two channels each, with no arguments.",
